<title>FRANCE: Algeria cuts discount rate by 1.0 point to 13 pct.</title>
<headline>Algeria cuts discount rate by 1.0 point to 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algerian central bank lowered the discount rate 1.0 point to 13 percent to spur economic growth, the official Algerian news agency said on Tuesday quoting the bank statement.</p>
<p>&quot;This reduction of interest rate initiates the easing of the interest rates applied to normative refinancing methods which are in phase with a decreasing inflation and the evolution of Algeria's monetary market,&quot; said the statement issued after the meeting of the bank's policy-making body, Credit and Monetary Council.</p>
</text>
